        "original_id": "383182fe-dae9-5127-b390-7fbe78c1fe5e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Clement Greenberg, Agatha Christie, Joseph Drapell, Jack Bush\n- Organizations: Cranbrook Academy, Ben's Bakery\n- Roles: visual art critic, essayist, crime novelist, short story writer, playwright, painter, artist\n- Concepts: American Modern art, pseudonyms\n- Works: Life (sculpture)\n\nFacts:\n- Agatha Christie was born on 15 September 1890 and died on 12 January 1976.\n- Agatha Christie was an English crime novelist, short story writer, and playwright.\n- Clement Greenberg was born on 16 January 1909 and died on 7 May 1994.\n- Clement Greenberg sometimes wrote under the pseudonym K. Hardesh.\n- Clement Greenberg was an American essayist and an influential visual art critic closely associated with mid-20th-century American Modern art.\n- At Cranbrook Academy, Joseph Drapell met visiting Canadian artist Jack Bush and American art critic Clement Greenberg, and both influenced Drapell's work.\n- In 1968, Ben's Bakery commissioned Life (sculpture), and painter Joseph Drapell produced it.",
